w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-name-imperium = Adaptive Reserve
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-name-heretics = Warp Flex Doctrine
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-brief-focus = Universal command profile.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-brief-effect = Stable cross-domain pacing with no hard early commitment.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-debuff = No direct stat debuff at the moment.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-summary = Neutral doctrine with no branch lock and no hard penalties.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-positive = Balanced profile: moderate boosts across all domains with no specialization lock.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-negative = Peak performance is lower than focused doctrines.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-lock = No branch is locked.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-full-briefing = Best for command teams that want to delay hard specialization until enemy tempo is clearer. This doctrine keeps all branches available and supports reactive planning across front, logistics, and research. It trades explosive peaks for consistency and lower strategic risk in uncertain openings.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-theme-imperium = Command keeps options open and delays hard specialization while scouting tempo.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-adaptive-reserve-theme-heretics = War council avoids binding itself to one creed and keeps tactical flexibility.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-name-imperium = Iron Forge
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-name-heretics = Blight Forge
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-brief-focus = Maximum engineering throughput.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-brief-effect = Pushes machine chains and production tempo to a hard peak.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-debuff = Reserved slot: possible frontline resilience penalty.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-summary = Hard engineering doctrine focused on machine throughput.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-positive = Strong engineering spike: faster machines and production chains.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-negative = Logistics and combat windows take an efficiency hit.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-lock = Locks branch: Research.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-full-briefing = Pick this when victory condition is backline momentum and sustained industrial pressure. It amplifies machine cadence and converts resources into output quickly, but the cost is lower flexibility in frontline and research response. The doctrine performs best when the team can protect infrastructure and play around production timings.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-theme-imperium = Mechanicus priority profile: resources are redirected into factory cadence and machine loops.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-iron-forge-theme-heretics = Ritual foundries are prioritized while frontline tempo adapts to forge output.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-name-imperium = Convoy Dominion
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-name-heretics = Blood Convoy
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-brief-focus = Supply flow and purchase bandwidth.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-brief-effect = Strengthens requisition stability and reduces backline downtime.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-debuff = Reserved slot: possible combat peak penalty.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-summary = Supply-focused doctrine for purchase capacity and ETA control.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-positive = Strong logistics spike: more purchase bandwidth and faster delivery windows.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-negative = Some combat and engineering outputs are reduced.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-lock = Locks branch: Research.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-full-briefing = Optimized for long rounds where logistics uptime decides frontline tempo. It improves procurement throughput, smooths supply cycles, and keeps rotation pressure consistent. Tradeoff is weaker burst potential in combat and engineering, so this doctrine rewards disciplined macro play and timing control.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-theme-imperium = Command holds momentum through uninterrupted resource flow and rotations.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-convoy-dominion-theme-heretics = Cult strategy overwhelms sectors through relentless convoy throughput.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-name-imperium = Lexmechanicus
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-name-heretics = Techno-Heresy Protocol
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-brief-focus = Research-driven late-stage control.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-brief-effect = Shifts power into technology synergy and decision quality.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-debuff = Reserved slot: possible logistics stability penalty.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-summary = Research-oriented doctrine built around late-stage tech synergies.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-positive = Strong research spike: better sustain profile and late combat control.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-negative = Lower logistics reserve and reduced engineering flexibility.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-lock = Locks branch: Logistics.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-full-briefing = Intended for teams planning to win through higher-quality systems rather than early tempo spikes. It improves long-fight control and late-phase consistency, but narrows logistics breathing room. Choose it only if your team can maintain supply discipline while investing into tech windows.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-theme-imperium = Analysts and tech-priests dictate the battle rhythm through strict protocol.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-lexmechanicus-theme-heretics = Heretek cadres take command, trading stable logistics for forbidden advantage.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-name-imperium = Spear of Assault
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-name-heretics = Breaker Fang
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-brief-focus = High-pressure assault profile.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-brief-effect = Increases frontline burst tempo and short-window lethality.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-debuff = Reserved slot: possible squad survivability penalty.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-summary = Aggressive breakthrough doctrine with high offensive pressure.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-positive = Strong combat spike: more damage and faster assault tempo.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-negative = Lower sustain reserve and reduced backline flexibility.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-lock = Locks branch: Logistics.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-full-briefing = Built for teams that want to break sectors before the enemy can stabilize. It enhances attack windows and rewards decisive pushes chained in short intervals. The downside is lower recovery depth if momentum stalls, so conversion of early pressure into map advantage is mandatory.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-theme-imperium = Command objective: break enemy structure before they can stabilize sectors.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-spear-of-assault-theme-heretics = Cult doctrine prioritizes slaughter pressure over long economy pacing.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-name-imperium = Void Bulwark
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-name-heretics = Unhallowed Bastion
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-brief-focus = Defensive endurance and line hold.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-brief-effect = Improves survivability cycles and positional stability.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-debuff = Reserved slot: possible offensive stat penalty.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-summary = Hold doctrine built around durability and positional control.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-positive = Strong defensive spike and better frontline recovery profile.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-negative = Reduced offensive output.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-lock = Locks branch: Engineering.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-full-briefing = Use this when your win path is attrition and territory denial. The doctrine boosts line durability, improves recovery discipline, and supports long defensive cycles under pressure. Tradeoff is slower offensive conversion, making timing of counter-pushes and zone control discipline critical.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-theme-imperium = Command grinds enemy tempo down through disciplined defense and rotation.
w40k-cmd-doctrine-void-bulwark-theme-heretics = Sector control through attrition, trading breakthrough speed for endurance.
